## 【Part 1: The Development Manifesto】## 1. Introduction: As Translators of Nature
Modern technology has successfully stabilized the "physical balance" of autonomous robots. However, it has repeatedly failed to embed the subtle, fluid essence of biological life within an artificial chassis of metal and code. Existing companion robots are charming, but they remain locked within pre-programmed, repetitive animation cycles. Human intuition instantly unmasks them as mere machines, eventually leading to consumer abandonment and emotional detachment.
『Curavita』 is an open-source, video-driven biomimetic robotics platform established to completely dismantle this paradigm.
We hold no arrogant ambitions of synthesizing "mechanical lifeforms." Instead, we operate with a profound respect for the organic locomotive patterns that nature has refined over millions of years. Our mission is to act as humble translators, utilizing advanced AI pipelines to precisely replicate (copy) these natural kinetics onto an artificial body.
By extracting biological locomotion profiles from millions of raw, unlabelled online videos (macro-movements) and combining them with minimal human fine-tuning (micro-skeletal coordinates), we have built a highly reliable synthesis framework. The result is an exquisite, mathematically rigorous replica of natural movement that rejects the cold, rigid repetition of traditional robotics, vibrating with the unpredictable and lifelike essence of real biology via compliance control and chaotic dynamics.
## 2. Core Philosophy: The Integrity of a "Zero-Camera" Architecture to Heal Loneliness
As we navigate an accelerating super-aged society and the rapid rise of single-person isolated households, we must ask: What should a true life partner look like?
Conventional robots mandate the integration of optical camera arrays to map environments and execute facial recognition. However, placing a continuous lens inside a private living space introduces an underlying layer of surveillance anxiety, violating individual privacy and compounding domestic stress.
Curavita completely eliminates optical cameras from its hardware (Zero-Camera Framework).
Deprived of vision, Curavita interacts with the world through alternate sensory channels: it listens to "voices," processes "odors," and senses surface textures via its "footpads (paw pads)." Upon entering a home, Curavita initially maintains a natural behavioral distance—displaying defensive behaviors such as pinning back its ears or tucking its tail via chaotic motion routines. Over a two-week acclimation period, it utilizes secure voiceprint and metabolic VOC pairing to identify its family members, gradually collapsing its behavioral boundaries.
Even within multi-person households, the system implements hierarchical processing mapped across biological groupings (children, grandparents, mother, father) and secondary chemical cross-checks to eliminate misidentification, maintaining an equitable, un-prioritized relationship with all occupants, just like a real biological pet.
This completely air-gapped, standalone architecture guarantees complete privacy, serving as the definitive legal and ethical solution required to deploy care companions seamlessly into single-person residences, hospitals, and assisted-living facilities.
## 3. A Sustainable Circular Economy: The Purpose of Caregiving
We refuse to treat Curavita as a disposable tech gadget. To eliminate financial barriers to entry, the total exclusion of vision processors and camera arrays lowers production bills of materials, enabling an accessible smartphone-tier retail price ("$350 to $500 / ¥50,000 to ¥70,000"). To secure long-term utility and corporate viability, we have integrated a sustainable maintenance infrastructure modeled after "Mandatory 3-Month Certified Salon Grooming."
Because the companion is treated as a family member, owners never endure the cold, clinical experience of shipping their companion in cardboard boxes. Instead, owners physically bring Curavita to a certified local salon, where a professional groomer manually cleans and brushes the artificial fur coat to restore its plush texture.
While the owner observes the grooming process, a certified technician opens a hidden underbelly hatch to safely swap worn internal joint buffers and battery cartridges, fulfilling all safety and verification protocols under Product Liability (PL) legislation. The boundary between the soft fur coat and the metallic sliding hatch is reinforced with fluororubber blades and molded labyrinth tracks, permanently maintaining an IP54 (Dust-protected, Splash-proof) ingress rating.
Owners who maintain a premium subscription consecutively for one year receive milestone rewards, such as a basic maintenance fee waiver and an in-person firmware update that uploads advanced behavioral growth profiles (e.g., rare vocalizations, specialized ear gestures, and nuanced affection routines) directly to the system memory. Guests visiting the household are seamlessly handled through a temporary, touch-activated mode that deploys visitor acoustics and VOCs to a secure, fully volatile RAM buffer, which physically purges all visitor footprints the instant Curavita docks at its nest. Furthermore, by tuning olfactory sensors to recognize generic chemical compounds (such as nepetalactone in silver vine or amino acid chains in pet treats) rather than proprietary corporate brands, Curavita safely bypasses trademark infringement boundaries, turning the established global pet food industry into powerful retail allies.
When dust or foreign objects collect on the wireless charging mat, Curavita generates a soft, plaintive whimpering sound, nudging the owner to clear its nest. Resting inside an open-walled "Theater-Basket" dock, the robot anchors its metallic underbelly cooling plate against the charging pad, allowing the owner to observe its peaceful sleeping postures at any time. This small act of wiping the nest, the trip to the local store to purchase treats, and the quarterly walk to the certified grooming salon form a cohesive UX design, transforming mandatory mechanical upkeep into rewarding caregiving rituals that structure the daily routines of isolated owners, restoring a vital sense of meaning and purpose to their lives.
## 4. To the Global Developer Community
Curavita is not a proprietary commercial product. It is a comprehensive, open-source architectural blueprint designed to migrate the kinetic souls of biological organisms into autonomous machines, spanning mathematical algorithms, embedded circuitry, structural mechanics, and circular service design.

* The development of edge-processing algorithms that classify road terrain profiles based on footpad pressure rise times without utilizing visual cameras.
* The design of fanless structural skeletons and underbelly convection plates that resolve thermal insulation issues caused by heavy fur coats without introducing acoustic fan noise.
* The execution of behavioral buffering scripts that transform sensor delay into realistic animal-like sniffing loops.

Let us unite our skills to build this technically rigorous, profoundly humane framework for artificial companion care. We invite programmers, circuit engineers, and 3D animators across the globe to consolidate their intelligence within our GitHub repositories.
Reclaim the vitality of care, once more in your hands.
—— Project Curavita
